      `it is prohibited by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is consistent with the Ideals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 2(2) the Court may do what it considers necessary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is an express provision in these Rules or any other written law on the matter`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is no express provision in these Rules or any other written law on any matter"
        IF `it is prohibited by law` OR (NOT `it is consistent with the Ideals`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as it is not prohibited by law and is consistent with the Ideals"
        IF `the Court considers it necessary on the facts to ensure that justice is done or to prevent an abuse of the process of the Court`
