`o 3 r 5(5) the period for the affidavit in opposition` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:337 | (5) If any party wishes to contest the application, the party must file and serve his or her affidavit within 14 days after being served with the
-- src:337 | application and affidavit.
@ref O 3 r 5(5) (src:337)
GIVEN `the party wishes to contest the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the party was served with the application and affidavit` IS A DATE
      `the date the affidavit is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the affidavit is served` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 5(5) the affidavit is filed and served within 14 days after service of the application` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party wishes to contest the application`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any party wishes to contest the application"
    ELSE
        `o 3 r 3 both of two acts are in time`
            (`o 3 r 3 the act is in time` `o 3 r 5(5) the period for the affidavit in opposition` `the date the party was served with the application and affidavit` `the date the affidavit is filed` calendar `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            (`o 3 r 3 the act is in time` `o 3 r 5(5) the period for the affidavit in opposition` `the date the party was served with the application and affidavit` `the date the affidavit is served` calendar `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)

-- src:338 | (6) Except in a special case, the Court will not allow further affidavits to be filed after the other party files his or her affidavit under paragraph
-- src:338 | (5).
@ref O 3 r 5(6) (src:338)
GIVEN `the other party has filed an affidavit under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 5(6) the Court allows a further affidavit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the other party has filed an affidavit under paragraph (5)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative applies "after the other party files his or her affidavit under paragraph (5)"
        IF `it is a special case`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Except in a special case" lifts the negative and does not say the Court will allow
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court will not allow further affidavits to be filed"

-- src:339 | (7) An affidavit must contain all necessary evidence in support of or in opposition (as the case may be) to the application, and may contain
-- src:339 | statements of information or belief with their sources and grounds clearly stated.
@ref O 3 r 5(7) (src:339)
GIVEN `the affidavit contains all necessary evidence in support of or in opposition to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any statement of information or belief in it has its source and grounds clearly stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 5(7) the affidavit has the content the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit contains all necessary evidence in support of or in opposition to the application` AND `any statement of information or belief in it has its source and grounds clearly stated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain all necessary evidence ... with their sources and grounds clearly stated"

-- src:340 | (8) All applications must be served on all other parties to the application except where the other party cannot or need not be served.
@ref O 3 r 5(8) (src:340)
GIVEN `the other party cannot or need not be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 5(8) the application must be served on the other party` MEANS
    IF `the other party cannot or need not be served`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where the other party cannot or need not be served"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Order 3, Rule 6 -- Forms`

-- src:342 | 6. —(1) The Forms as set out in the practice directions must be used with such variations as the circumstances require.
@ref O 3 r 6(1) (src:342)
GIVEN `a Form for the document is set out in the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variations made are only those the circumstances require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 6(1) the Form must be used with the variations the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF `a Form for the document is set out in the practice directions` AND `the variations made are only those the circumstances require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Forms as set out in the practice directions ... with such variations as the circumstances require"

DECLARE `o 3 r 6(2) who approves a variation` IS ONE OF
    `o 3 r 6(2) the Chief Justice approves`
    `o 3 r 6(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts approves`
    `o 3 r 6(2) nobody has approved`

-- src:342 | (2) The Forms may be varied by practice directions issued with the approval of the Chief Justice or with the approval of the Presiding Judge of the
-- src:342 | State Courts, as the case may be.
@ref O 3 r 6(2) (src:342)
GIVEN `the practice directions are issued by the Registrar of` IS A `Court system`
      approval IS A `o 3 r 6(2) who approves a variation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 6(2) the Forms are varied by practice directions` MEANS
    CONSIDER approval
    WHEN `o 3 r 6(2) the Chief Justice approves` THEN
        IF `the practice directions are issued by the Registrar of` EQUALS `Supreme Court` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as the case may be"
    WHEN `o 3 r 6(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts approves` THEN
        IF `the practice directions are issued by the Registrar of` EQUALS `State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as the case may be"
    WHEN `o 3 r 6(2) nobody has approved` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be varied by practice directions issued with the approval of the Chief Justice or ... the Presiding Judge of the State Courts"

-- src:343 | (3) Where a Form states “Seal of the Court”, a document in that Form must bear the seal of the Court.
@ref O 3 r 6(3) (src:343)
GIVEN `the Form states "Seal of the Court"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 6(3) the document must bear the seal of the Court` MEANS
    IF `the Form states "Seal of the Court"`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a Form states “Seal of the Court”"

§§ `Order 3, Rule 7 -- language of documents`

-- src:345 | 7. —(1) All documents filed or used in Court must be in the English language.
@ref O 3 r 7(1) (src:345)
GIVEN `the document is filed or used in Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 7(1) the document filed or used in Court is in the English language as required` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is filed or used in Court`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for "All documents filed or used in Court"
    ELSE IF `the document is in the English language`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in the English language"

-- src:345 | (2) A document which is not in the English language must be accompanied by a translation in the English language certified by a court interpreter or
-- src:345 | verified by an affidavit of a person qualified to translate the document.
@ref O 3 r 7(2) (src:345)
GIVEN `the document is not in the English language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the translation is certified by a court interpreter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the translation is verified by an affidavit of a person qualified to translate the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 7(2) the document not in English is accompanied by a certified or verified translation` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is not in the English language`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for "A document which is not in the English language"
    ELSE IF `the translation is certified by a court interpreter` OR `the translation is verified by an affidavit of a person qualified to translate the document`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a translation in the English language certified by a court interpreter or verified by an affidavit"

§§ `Order 3, Rule 8 -- foreign documents under the Apostille Convention or a Civil Procedure Convention`

-- src:347-348 | Despite anything in these Rules, the following documents may be received, filed or used in the Court: ( a ) a foreign public document with an
-- src:347-348 | apostille placed on or attached to it;
@ref O 3 r 8(1)(a) (src:347-348)
GIVEN `the document is a foreign public document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an apostille is placed on or attached to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 8(1)(a) the document may be received, filed or used in the Court as a foreign public document with an apostille` MEANS
    IF `the document is a foreign public document` AND `an apostille is placed on or attached to it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists documents that "may be received, filed or used" and does not say others may not

-- src:350 | a document or a translation of the document that has been drawn up or certified, and duly sealed, by a court or other competent authority of a foreign
-- src:350 | country, being a country with which there subsists a Civil Procedure Convention providing for the dispensation of the authentication of such
-- src:350 | documents.
@ref O 3 r 8(1)(b) (src:350)
GIVEN `the document or translation is drawn up or certified, and duly sealed, by a court or other competent authority of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Civil Procedure Convention providing for the dispensation of the authentication of such documents subsists with that country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 8(1)(b) the document may be received, filed or used in the Court under a Civil Procedure Convention` MEANS
    IF `the document or translation is drawn up or certified, and duly sealed, by a court or other competent authority of a foreign country` AND `a Civil Procedure Convention providing for the dispensation of the authentication of such documents subsists with that country`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists documents that "may be received, filed or used" and does not say others may not

-- Rule 8(2): both terms are handed to the Apostille Act 2020, which is not among the sources: the answer is asked as an input.
-- src:351 | “apostille” means a Convention certificate as defined by section 10 of the Apostille Act 2020;
