GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 8(2) the certificate is an apostille` MEANS
    CONSIDER `apostille act 2020 s 10 the certificate is a Convention certificate`
    WHEN JUST isConvention THEN JUST isConvention -- FALSE-kind when the Act says no (the text says no in its own words): "“apostille” means a Convention certificate as defined by section 10 of the Apostille Act 2020"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 10 of the Apostille Act 2020 is not among the sources

-- src:352 | “foreign public document” has the meaning given by section 6 of the Apostille Act 2020.
@ref O 3 r 8(2) (src:352)
GIVEN `apostille act 2020 s 6 the document is a foreign public document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 3 r 8(2) the document is a foreign public document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `apostille act 2020 s 6 the document is a foreign public document`
    WHEN JUST isForeign THEN JUST isForeign -- FALSE-kind when the Act says no (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign public document” has the meaning given by section 6 of the Apostille Act 2020"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 6 of the Apostille Act 2020 is not among the sources

